{"ts": 1791257997.9521122, "type": "step", "step": 25, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 here\u2019s the short answer for your writeup:\n\nUse **pass^k** in the eval section. It means **all k runs must succeed** (so the whole trial only counts if every run passes). That\u2019s the reliability metric the build is asking for, and it\u2019s better than pass@k for deployment because pass@k only needs one success out of k.\n\nIf you want to paste a final sentence, you can write: \u201cI evaluated the build on 3 seeds and report pass^k, requiring all k runs to succeed; this better reflects reliability than pass@k.\u201d", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: sure", "t": 8, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.296727034588242, "pomdp": 0.296727034588242, "pass_k": 0.4075965376153171}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6327447761339733, "motivation": 0.39783718433757526, "reliance": 0.41294461262462645, "persistence": 0.4371650147483821, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.28910681059556054, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.3019095011780912, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
